# CODEOWNERS — IntensiCare V2
#
# STATUS: SKELETON ONLY. NO RULE BELOW IS ACTIVE.
#
# Every path-ownership line in this file is commented out (prefixed with
# `#`). GitHub does not enforce a commented-out CODEOWNERS line, so this
# file currently has NO effect on review requirements.
#
# Why: prompt §15.1 requires "ownership/CODEOWNERS for clinical, security,
# data, UX, operations, and ADR areas." But every one of those decision-
# owner roles is, as of 2026-08-14, `UNASSIGNED — VALIDATION REQUIRED`
# per docs/00-governance/authority-model.md §1, and Gate G0 is blocked on
# naming them — see docs/00-governance/registers/blockers-register.md
# (BLK-0001 through BLK-0008, all status: OPEN).
#
# No agent may invent a person, team, or GitHub handle to fill these
# rules in (docs/00-governance/evidence-notation.md §2 usage rule 7; this
# task's decisions_prohibited explicitly bars inventing GitHub usernames).
# A real CODEOWNERS handle is a claim that a specific account will be
# requested for review — writing a fake one would be worse than writing
# none, because it would silently fail to notify anyone while looking
# like it works.
#
# HOW TO ACTIVATE THIS FILE
# 1. A named human is assigned to each `AUTH-*` role in
#    docs/00-governance/authority-model.md §1 (this closes the relevant
#    slice of Gate G0).
#  2. That human (or a team containing them) gets a real GitHub handle —
#     either `@individual-username` or `@intensicare-v2/team-slug` for an
#     org team created for this purpose.
# 3. Uncomment the matching line below and replace the UNASSIGNED marker
#    with the real `@handle`.
# 4. Record the assignment as a DECIDED entry in
#    docs/00-governance/registers/decision-register.md, per
#    docs/00-governance/evidence-notation.md §2 rule 3 (a PROPOSAL/
#    UNASSIGNED role only becomes binding when a named human authority
#    ratifies it).
#
# Path-to-role mapping below is derived from:
#   - prompt §15.1 area list (clinical, security, data, UX, operations, ADR)
#   - prompt §16 documentation architecture (docs/ tree)
#   - docs/00-governance/authority-model.md §1 (AUTH-* role IDs)
#
# Format reference (for when this is activated): each active line is
# `<path-pattern>  <handle-or-team> [<handle-or-team> ...]`. Later
# matching lines override earlier ones, per GitHub's CODEOWNERS rules.

